we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]+(2t-3)[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8t-2 \\\\ 6t+4 \\\\ 10t+12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8t-12 \\\\ 6t-9 \\\\ 10t-15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71225/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71225"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70685/selection/4ff5e6b6eff2844a5dfed9e6f82d0491061fa1dc5c52d560dc6ab89639d9f7b7" :answer/id #uuid "37e660d1-908e-5666-b5d8-ca26033bf504" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{3}{{t}^{3}}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70685/selection/9b64eafc5a582544d20c9b346181d34aad83de466cad3729e418795f955027a7" :answer/id #uuid "2c0f1574-1851-5686-8819-5ccd95e3ed2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70685/selection/c413fbbb40fb282c4c9fb40f67d4f179153e7142e150e36829c9ad71073b1261" :answer/id #uuid "2e7c6caa-889e-5dc8-b553-a6ecbb6f8a56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70685/selection/8e1a7e66181ab461855e7a3b98aa624163c138fe4c995c929bbd9b157607d2cf" :answer/id #uuid "ebea4dd2-a8e6-5c3d-88b1-c9f0f7b3149d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70685/selection/631f79c409d7a4cf35f29d5a19c56bb01a062924bb85ed3f7e63955106677df9" :answer/id #uuid "37438a7a-6ec2-5c6b-a483-3116933fb3ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ {t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{3}+3t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70685/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a25d6d17-d8b2-5b92-bde2-a8f121e43643" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70685/selection/c413fbbb40fb282c4c9fb40f67d4f179153e7142e150e36829c9ad71073b1261" :answer-field/choices ["q-70685/selection/4ff5e6b6eff2844a5dfed9e6f82d0491061fa1dc5c52d560dc6ab89639d9f7b7" "q-70685/selection/9b64eafc5a582544d20c9b346181d34aad83de466cad3729e418795f955027a7" "q-70685/selection/c413fbbb40fb282c4c9fb40f67d4f179153e7142e150e36829c9ad71073b1261" "q-70685/selection/8e1a7e66181ab461855e7a3b98aa624163c138fe4c995c929bbd9b157607d2cf" "q-70685/selection/631f79c409d7a4cf35f29d5a19c56bb01a062924bb85ed3f7e63955106677df9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70685" :question/id #uuid "a2951dd3-82c4-5618-8df7-28388cc279c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-70685" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ t \\\\ {t}^{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-70685/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70685"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32498"] :question/problem "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}2u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=2t+2$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(2u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2(2t+2) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-33260/selection/21b9cd2886e630323b09aa7e0295eb6743c289c5f6cac13850a2f17f4add5831" :answer/id #uuid "cb6f1b81-3a1c-50da-a2e3-89884eb7b89c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33260/selection/603b17267fcdf1d3d7d81ec4248299124049343e383ebc3ea22226fa6d469ddf" :answer/id #uuid "4df4329c-21d2-51a8-b053-05bb883f4820" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33260/selection/bb25032004adcadd34b0836f012089e330b5eef00de355d14826b0a8766d8c94" :answer/id #uuid "4b6c3d1f-8052-5990-80a0-a5b0872c3f23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+6t{e}^{2t}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33260/selection/bb65d4bd09a94aed135e10e04d1f460c9c83ab721ddb34795f14443323235d30" :answer/id #uuid "76ca5026-3449-5cf6-9238-64cc4803d070" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{e}^{2t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{4t}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33260/selection/1290c4a03ce3f21f983d24dd6e7e0e667f43d8089c5c1f3567f3523c3a62d7f3" :answer/id #uuid "e6ef7c57-c032-526f-aa67-9b807706273d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i-8{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33260/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "df0dcda6-9c3c-5e46-bfc9-36ecd5a93d63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33260/selection/603b17267fcdf1d3d7d81ec4248299124049343e383ebc3ea22226fa6d469ddf" :answer-field/choices ["q-33260/selection/21b9cd2886e630323b09aa7e0295eb6743c289c5f6cac13850a2f17f4add5831" "q-33260/selection/603b17267fcdf1d3d7d81ec4248299124049343e383ebc3ea22226fa6d469ddf" "q-33260/selection/bb25032004adcadd34b0836f012089e330b5eef00de355d14826b0a8766d8c94" "q-33260/selection/bb65d4bd09a94aed135e10e04d1f460c9c83ab721ddb34795f14443323235d30" "q-33260/selection/1290c4a03ce3f21f983d24dd6e7e0e667f43d8089c5c1f3567f3523c3a62d7f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33260" :question/id #uuid "9342327c-ff4e-553a-a4f4-0263c91cce83" :question/math-academy-id "q-33260" :question/problem "If $f(u)={e}^{u+1}\\,i+{e}^{2u}\\,j+\\frac{1}{e}\\,k$ and $u(t)=2{t}^{2}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)=f′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u+1})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{2u})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\frac{1}{e}\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2u}\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})=4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\ (f∘u)^{′}(t) & =({e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+2{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j)4t \\\\  & =4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-33260/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33260"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32869/selection/7a5a4d9d06529e60735e649b92d7565b0098400390173191e789186ff12c2d9e" :answer/id #uuid "da588f43-0186-5c7d-b8cc-759c93d2cd8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-2t},\\,0,\\,{e}^{-4t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32869/selection/c089f1544be5ef64921911035e528a4b8f075de026615d9f49cf7ec3d2996f3f" :answer/id #uuid "c81cf2d5-da0f-577f-b402-8d0d0b0fef74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-2t},\\,0,\\,-{e}^{-4t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32869/selection/054a07da1ea6705d5a9a28e90a6124cca7e0cdba3d47ee5d3fefaf110fd822a2" :answer/id #uuid "51a6f446-26c9-5cf0-aa92-48ea3c2c01b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{2t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32869/selection/440be9fe68774b2e78be150485fd8780519c4030dffcdcd908fbb050a411ee8f" :answer/id #uuid "48c9cf06-5155-534b-94d5-3460987103d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32869/selection/e9def05a06b6fb342b498b6f870b5888ed2c9c1aebc6d8fdbe645bfd32c89050" :answer/id #uuid "13fe3f9d-fcda-5a0d-b6c2-8ea7b22cb170" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32869/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf2cfbcb-f670-5fa4-a986-b61b9f1f0188" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32869/selection/440be9fe68774b2e78be150485fd8780519c4030dffcdcd908fbb050a411ee8f" :answer-field/choices ["q-32869/selection/7a5a4d9d06529e60735e649b92d7565b0098400390173191e789186ff12c2d9e" "q-32869/selection/c089f1544be5ef64921911035e528a4b8f075de026615d9f49cf7ec3d2996f3f" "q-32869/selection/054a07da1ea6705d5a9a28e90a6124cca7e0cdba3d47ee5d3fefaf110fd822a2" "q-32869/selection/440be9fe68774b2e78be150485fd8780519c4030dffcdcd908fbb050a411ee8f" "q-32869/selection/e9def05a06b6fb342b498b6f870b5888ed2c9c1aebc6d8fdbe645bfd32c89050"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32869" :question/id #uuid "3070a9d8-58c0-56d5-a223-11b2e4bdf7ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-32869" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{u}⟩$ and $u(t)={e}^{2t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}0,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})=2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u(t)},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}(t)}⟩{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}⟨\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{({e}^{2t})^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{4t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-32869/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32869"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128570/selection/a4c288e79fb738096e0adc07a171eb8e9fedb6cecb99c4e96491490bd0a2df88" :answer/id #uuid "4e255fc7-6272-5f92-82e3-d5da680cb14a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{t},-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128570/selection/5d78fc2bbe7e881959cd7fedc77a9c74012444bda05c865c404e615d2398f517" :answer/id #uuid "eb1bba33-58b4-5a00-b06a-ff91a11fd24a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128570/selection/c101f2406fd1838226f11c0520697fde454e658c9a67d1003e4c23d4a0a6275a" :answer/id #uuid "c3894f94-e78d-54bc-9274-7c41774f70f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{t}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128570/selection/2b8660d7523c8d8e191b8db3a83f1536111358d2383038778f815369e6c7974e" :answer/id #uuid "e1688504-491d-5ed1-977d-71a2be217a97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,-\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128570/selection/3c0ad87a011967a044eec4f4358e73a62b0f9f7c61a98a9ad6ab6c454af8538a" :answer/id #uuid "83e2f4cf-588a-592d-9565-6a6c5ef07e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128570/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "00777e8c-8742-506c-8fd2-c313410fdbd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128570/selection/5d78fc2bbe7e881959cd7fedc77a9c74012444bda05c865c404e615d2398f517" :answer-field/choices ["q-128570/selection/a4c288e79fb738096e0adc07a171eb8e9fedb6cecb99c4e96491490bd0a2df88" "q-128570/selection/5d78fc2bbe7e881959cd7fedc77a9c74012444bda05c865c404e615d2398f517" "q-128570/selection/c101f2406fd1838226f11c0520697fde454e658c9a67d1003e4c23d4a0a6275a" "q-128570/selection/2b8660d7523c8d8e191b8db3a83f1536111358d2383038778f815369e6c7974e" "q-128570/selection/3c0ad87a011967a044eec4f4358e73a62b0f9f7c61a98a9ad6ab6c454af8538a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128570" :question/id #uuid "00ec801b-e22a-5c19-899f-45b6911ab4a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128570" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1),\\,1⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u+1},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(u(t))^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)+1},\\,0⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{t}{1+t},\\,0⟩\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128570/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32860/selection/22fdf27b52204fb6edbd191d96960dd9d58fd0c62939869af3990b64ebe90839" :answer/id #uuid "ce329a3c-d6dc-516e-8f1d-f962832405f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32860/selection/d57e1c1f1462c98d62711eb2ab824f43858a50e60f6997aabb469933f36ad02e" :answer/id #uuid "5291c699-50fe-522f-a333-7bba287e5b23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32860/selection/1b48bcb5ebf288ed47e3f6824788582e2becb73ae6c9dd3599a80b1b7b911f8b" :answer/id #uuid "42b63046-d0c8-5b17-a680-40625cee930b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32860/selection/956c2aa0f5bef377ab28b2c8f16f3a38521a87a6468528db548ef1bcedf1ac9b" :answer/id #uuid "f210782f-76de-5c66-920d-d343470da810" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32860/selection/405a24de355abe2582fd0e7ce5c6513145ddc9249f46830250c778acc5e66e38" :answer/id #uuid "059f6fed-d4b0-5135-99a2-3f4b6890742c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32860/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e243c6fc-094b-525d-978b-2c3f8f5a01d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32860/selection/22fdf27b52204fb6edbd191d96960dd9d58fd0c62939869af3990b64ebe90839" :answer-field/choices ["q-32860/selection/22fdf27b52204fb6edbd191d96960dd9d58fd0c62939869af3990b64ebe90839" "q-32860/selection/d57e1c1f1462c98d62711eb2ab824f43858a50e60f6997aabb469933f36ad02e" "q-32860/selection/1b48bcb5ebf288ed47e3f6824788582e2becb73ae6c9dd3599a80b1b7b911f8b" "q-32860/selection/956c2aa0f5bef377ab28b2c8f16f3a38521a87a6468528db548ef1bcedf1ac9b" "q-32860/selection/405a24de355abe2582fd0e7ce5c6513145ddc9249f46830250c778acc5e66e38"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32860" :question/id #uuid "24bb40b1-a7b7-5eea-a633-757e31425152" :question/math-academy-id "q-32860" :question/problem "If $g(u)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ 5 \\\\ {u}^{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t$, then  $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,5\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,{u}^{2}\\,\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u(t)} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u(t)\\end{aligned}]{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-32860/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32860"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128587/selection/5c720045ac78552aa86a7d319f1126b3706438cf66738908b68799580422fe62" :answer/id #uuid "eb032af8-4753-5ccb-8d9c-fe6e52cbfdd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{3},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128587/selection/e96c9cc6cfc686a04f74c43ff1d3c70aac07fec34284ed29665987f5281db83b" :answer/id #uuid "86827724-76b1-54de-aa37-b7f9adb2fc3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{2},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128587/selection/486c3978431882a31ee8d7727b488511c1ad963dc6704a7396e707262d635f69" :answer/id #uuid "2d708fa5-55b2-5152-8aaa-26338dd6cb84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128587/selection/fb3198392cb46e5ff66ac619507c7acdc6ea458a9be8a53b04a27dbc4de5188f" :answer/id #uuid "81ac5ec6-6a72-5ffd-88df-5fc2b2b99163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128587/selection/c4842f0e2121cc0578ea25bdfed668d8f21156ba8a609f463d23605e30fe9103" :answer/id #uuid "3875e15b-7b54-591c-a1ea-95ddfd8b539a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{4},\\,3{t}^{5}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128587/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6d9e1d3-65a6-5f96-b7c3-5deec932ff21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128587/selection/fb3198392cb46e5ff66ac619507c7acdc6ea458a9be8a53b04a27dbc4de5188f" :answer-field/choices ["q-128587/selection/5c720045ac78552aa86a7d319f1126b3706438cf66738908b68799580422fe62" "q-128587/selection/e96c9cc6cfc686a04f74c43ff1d3c70aac07fec34284ed29665987f5281db83b" "q-128587/selection/486c3978431882a31ee8d7727b488511c1ad963dc6704a7396e707262d635f69" "q-128587/selection/fb3198392cb46e5ff66ac619507c7acdc6ea458a9be8a53b04a27dbc4de5188f" "q-128587/selection/c4842f0e2121cc0578ea25bdfed668d8f21156ba8a609f463d23605e30fe9103"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128587" :question/id #uuid "9d5f8c70-9278-5162-973d-4d7fea2c16c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-128587" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(ug(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{3}⟨1,\\,2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩+3{t}^{2}⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,2{t}^{4},\\,6{t}^{5}⟩+⟨3{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{4},\\,6{t}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128587/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128587"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32298"] :question/problem "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k \\\\ g(t) & ={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(20t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k)\\cdot ({t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k)+(20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(20{t}^{3}-2t+5({t}^{2}+t))+(60{t}^{3}-2t+(2+5t)(2t+1)) \\\\  & =80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-128586/selection/2122b1dc02e1205f6497662765b71daf3d7fdf86ffed0a21849698d12aa20c6f" :answer/id #uuid "85521d67-6236-51ea-8ce7-d15513094f2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128586/selection/cfc8ed980e35d84b0767f1edaafef2103a702069b46540ae4e296422caf93ec3" :answer/id #uuid "dc1fd693-aa78-5dfd-a34d-37c50e3cef97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,t,\\,3t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128586/selection/1781c038436cb26b97aebab0d982ac4a86e3cacb0d506651ebaf0e6ce7479e7d" :answer/id #uuid "50dc45cb-e55b-52f4-a52b-5bece1dec1ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128586/selection/1979ba45cc9a1709e9a0432cb811d00bf95a6e8972599eb61648efe7f6ef8550" :answer/id #uuid "29a1d4dc-da17-5066-9630-3494aaf14753" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128586/selection/910ac568cc3d68599b88142ca3ba0aab16c0557153319fb88844e0bb1ee40a47" :answer/id #uuid "3e4de446-e262-5377-9584-38c04d82f392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128586/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "63cfc577-b71b-52e8-a8a3-1261487aa5c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128586/selection/910ac568cc3d68599b88142ca3ba0aab16c0557153319fb88844e0bb1ee40a47" :answer-field/choices ["q-128586/selection/2122b1dc02e1205f6497662765b71daf3d7fdf86ffed0a21849698d12aa20c6f" "q-128586/selection/cfc8ed980e35d84b0767f1edaafef2103a702069b46540ae4e296422caf93ec3" "q-128586/selection/1781c038436cb26b97aebab0d982ac4a86e3cacb0d506651ebaf0e6ce7479e7d" "q-128586/selection/1979ba45cc9a1709e9a0432cb811d00bf95a6e8972599eb61648efe7f6ef8550" "q-128586/selection/910ac568cc3d68599b88142ca3ba0aab16c0557153319fb88844e0bb1ee40a47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128586" :question/id #uuid "bf8c3fb4-2777-54a7-8b95-c44fdfa25968" :question/math-academy-id "q-128586" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ and $v(t)=2t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t,\\,1⟩+2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,4{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩+⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128586/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128586"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128896/selection/2215f4ec688513a587d357c6500116bc1ecb1aec61c829d0ab5c4c730ebf859e" :answer/id #uuid "9e01d9a9-2a90-5a58-9d87-627daa5da8c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{6}-5,\\,4{t}^{5}+2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128896/selection/045cafbdd2a6430371b0accea393373e517d5fe6b17449627c8281de589ed397" :answer/id #uuid "a27ec2ea-c098-5486-8483-fa7df003a644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨5{t}^{6},\\,{t}^{5}+4{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128896/selection/8db372f46138da224ea2d7a8e2dc47f6d43e99f93e030e3bdd822a85e1136fa9" :answer/id #uuid "9bb993ab-caa1-5bbc-a46e-6b91afb5baad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨7{t}^{6},\\,6{t}^{5}-5,\\,4{t}^{3}+2t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128896/selection/55398bd9d1b20589ef600bd7669604db032fcd1f3701c69d57083972ca96734e" :answer/id #uuid "25744ee0-8070-50f2-9184-27b0c4af738b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128896/selection/2662e08ab22d3c718f1c01bd0141ce794fdae4f3c308b78be622e402b47cb13f" :answer/id #uuid "07f384ad-9b9f-524a-9131-9ac57b5fbc9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{t}^{6}+1,\\,4{t}^{5},\\,{t}^{3}-5t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128896/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ad2398b-cb23-53c5-a1bc-3850caae08ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128896/selection/55398bd9d1b20589ef600bd7669604db032fcd1f3701c69d57083972ca96734e" :answer-field/choices ["q-128896/selection/2215f4ec688513a587d357c6500116bc1ecb1aec61c829d0ab5c4c730ebf859e" "q-128896/selection/045cafbdd2a6430371b0accea393373e517d5fe6b17449627c8281de589ed397" "q-128896/selection/8db372f46138da224ea2d7a8e2dc47f6d43e99f93e030e3bdd822a85e1136fa9" "q-128896/selection/55398bd9d1b20589ef600bd7669604db032fcd1f3701c69d57083972ca96734e" "q-128896/selection/2662e08ab22d3c718f1c01bd0141ce794fdae4f3c308b78be622e402b47cb13f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128896" :question/id #uuid "c21f1368-688b-50ed-bde8-7422d801bdbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-128896" :question/problem "Find $(f\\times g)^{′}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨t,\\,5,\\,{t}^{4}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\times g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t)+f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3} & t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{3} & t\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & t\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\,4{t}^{5}-t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩, \\\\ f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ t & 5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}t & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}t & 5 \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\,2{t}^{5}-t,\\,3{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\times g)^{′}(t) & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\,4{t}^{5}-t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩+⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\,2{t}^{5}-t,\\,3{t}^{3}-10t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-128896/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128896"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32837/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "1256526b-0b63-5849-ba74-47a5ae991c40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32837/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "0a79529c-5c53-5eef-866f-9e91c6e4d092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32837/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "bbc82d85-4371-53f6-b5fc-69fcb54c1cc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32837/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "f750d2e5-0984-584e-bf6c-4a6db0237a73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32837/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "ca2411e2-bdce-546a-ab4b-2d46ff1b9b3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32837/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d90a3398-318a-588b-8110-fc4ea12ba2c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32837/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-32837/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" "q-32837/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-32837/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-32837/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-32837/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32837" :question/id #uuid "d5473c95-fbd9-54b5-ab3e-4d48d13acc31" :question/math-academy-id "q-32837" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+4{t}^{2}\\,k$, evaluate $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+4\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+8t\\,k \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2t\\,i+2j+8\\,k \\\\  & =6t\\,i+2j+8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0) & ={f}^{″}(0)\\cdot f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)\\cdot {f}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =(6(0)\\,i+2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (({0}^{3}-1)\\,i+({0}^{2}-2)\\,j+4(0)^{2}\\,k)+(3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k)\\cdot (3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k) \\\\  & =(2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (-i-2\\,j) \\\\  & =0(-1)+2(-2)+(0) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32837/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32837"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-2477"] :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-2478"] :question/problem "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where $[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t) = t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-2479"] :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-2480"] :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
